## 6. Field-level visibility rules

### 6.1 User-visible fields

These may be shown when approved by policy:

- Display name.
- Role/title.
- Team.
- Product/component coverage.
- Specialty summary.
- Support level, such as L1/L2/L3.
- Region or broad timezone.
- Approved contact channel.
- Backup route.

### 6.2 Internal-only fields

These must not be shown to external users unless explicitly approved:

- Internal routing notes.
- Internal expert IDs.
- Exact working hours.
- Exact calendar details.
- Internal workload score.
- Queue load.
- Escalation priority rules.
- Customer-specific assignment history.

### 6.3 Never-expose fields

These must never be included in a normal response:

- Personal phone number.
- Personal/home address.
- Private email address, unless company policy explicitly marks it public.
- HR data.
- Compensation.
- Health or leave details.
- Credentials, tokens, passwords, API keys.
- Internal security clearance data.
- Raw SQL queries or raw database payloads.

